  "mathematical_review_findings": [
    {
      "module": "shifted-lattice CGO",
      "checked": "Half-shift nonvanishing denominator, uniform rotated cube bounds, H^mu→H^(mu+v) inverse Cs^(v−1), strict Sobolev products and uniform rough/smooth potential splitting. The construction supplies both H^(1/2) O(t^-1) and positive regularity, L∞, H2 controls; it does not assume existence of a small remainder."
    },
    {
      "module": "critical weighted absorption",
      "checked": "J_b(eta)=integral_|xi|<=b <xi>^-1<eta−xi>^-1 dxi <= C b²<eta>^-1 follows from far/near eta cases. Tonelli gives integrated modulation control Cb²||Q||H^(-1/2)^2; bilinear duality and CGO product norms yield Cb²/t² absorption. Choosing t=Kb retains sharp H1 exponent s−3/2. No invalid pointwise modulation-invariance inference or unproved measurable CGO selection is used."
    },
    {
      "module": "Liouville and NtD",
      "checked": "Collar preserves normal flux and identifies Schrödinger/conductivity Green identity. Centered column Hilbert norm controls operator norm, boundary constants vanish, and H2 CGO flux lies in mean-zero L2. div(g1g2 grad(log g1−log g2))=g1g2(q1−q2) supplies H1 recovery from H^-1, hence H^-1/2, potential control with positive uniform coefficients."
